WEBVTT

00:00:00.422 --> 00:00:04.268
This is LaneDesk, a small CRM built for a freight sales agent.

00:00:04.268 --> 00:00:10.161
It is one screen for the whole day: who to call, what was promised, and which loads are moving.

00:00:10.161 --> 00:00:13.201
Let's sign in and walk through a typical morning.

00:00:14.203 --> 00:00:15.715
This is the Today screen.

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:19.223
At the top are the day's targets, calls and conversations.

00:00:19.223 --> 00:00:22.308
Below are follow-ups that are due, and a call list.

00:00:22.308 --> 00:00:28.114
The call list only shows people who are inside business hours right now, in their own time zone.

00:00:28.114 --> 00:00:35.856
The clock next to each name is their local time, so you never wake someone up in Denver or call Honolulu at five in the morning.

00:00:36.858 --> 00:00:38.764
Logging a call takes one click.

00:00:38.764 --> 00:00:43.191
Pacific Rim Electronics did not pick up last time, so I click Voicemail.

00:00:43.191 --> 00:00:48.847
The row disappears, the call is recorded, and the next follow up is scheduled automatically.

00:00:48.847 --> 00:00:50.876
The same works for the call list.

00:00:50.876 --> 00:00:52.167
Talked to a prospect?

00:00:52.167 --> 00:00:54.565
One click, and it is on their timeline.

00:00:55.568 --> 00:00:58.318
For a longer conversation, open the company.

00:00:58.318 --> 00:01:00.880
Lone Star Building Supply wants flatbeds.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:06.193
I pick who I spoke to, choose when to follow up, type a quick note, and click Talked.

00:01:06.193 --> 00:01:11.568
That is three clicks, and the timeline updates right away, without reloading the page.

00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:14.716
Now the customer asks for a price.

00:01:14.716 --> 00:01:22.479
From the company page I quote a load: Dallas to Kansas City, flatbed, forty thousand pounds, at twenty one hundred dollars.

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:29.232
The form refuses weights above forty eight thousand pounds, the legal limit, so a typo cannot slip through.

00:01:30.233 --> 00:01:33.376
The pipeline shows every load from quote to delivery.

00:01:33.376 --> 00:01:35.629
The customer says yes, so I click Won.

00:01:35.629 --> 00:01:39.661
To cover the load I choose a carrier and enter what I will pay them.

00:01:39.661 --> 00:01:43.041
The margin appears instantly, four hundred fifty dollars.

00:01:43.041 --> 00:01:47.666
Then one click when the truck is picked up, and one more when it is delivered.

00:01:47.666 --> 00:01:52.825
A load cannot be covered without a carrier, and cannot be marked lost without a reason.

00:01:53.827 --> 00:01:56.103
Some companies must never be called.

00:01:56.103 --> 00:01:58.885
Bayou Chemical Supply is marked Do Not Call.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:06.030
The company page shows a clear warning, the call form is gone, and the company never appears on the Today screen.

00:02:07.031 --> 00:02:15.295
The Stats screen shows how the week is going against your targets: calls, conversations, quotes and loads, your win rate, and your margin.

00:02:15.295 --> 00:02:20.983
Commission is calculated from the margin using your percentage, for the week and for the month.

00:02:21.985 --> 00:02:23.726
Coming from a spreadsheet?

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:26.807
Import companies and contacts from a CSV file.

00:02:26.807 --> 00:02:31.628
Duplicates are detected by MC number, or by name and state, and skipped.

00:02:31.628 --> 00:02:36.919
Bad rows are reported with the line number instead of failing the whole import.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:44.752
That is LaneDesk: call, quote, cover, deliver, and see your numbers, on one screen, with almost no clicking.

00:02:44.752 --> 00:02:45.890
This is phase one.

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:49.432
The voice in this video is synthetic, generated locally.

00:02:49.432 --> 00:02:52.342
Thanks for watching, and please send feedback.

